{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:d80efac571afb3e2","name":"Security Personnel","source":{"id":"source:reference-d80efac571afb3e2","title":"Security Personnel","revision":19021,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:09:14Z","sha256":"737452e4b569b3b029ebe52294b8b06aa6580589328db4f130da05db6be21f32","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19021","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Security%20Personnel&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-d80efac571afb3e2","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The galaxy is a dangerous place, filled with all sorts of nasty characters. As a result, security is one of the primary concerns for most people of wealth, prestige, and power. To protect against villainy and to safeguard the common citizen against crime, governments maintain extensive security forces. These groups often consist of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Police Officers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Police_Officers"}," who patrol the streets on foot or through the air in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeders","referenceId":"reference:8831ac17fd67f6fc"},". Like military units, Security Personnel typically follow a rigid rank structure. With guards outranked by detectives, sergeants, and so on all the way to the commander at the top.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Security Personnel are not restricted to law enforcement agencies. These characters can also represent the personal security forces of powerful figures in the galaxy. Security Personnel might be private soldiers of a Corporate Sector czar or the armed guards of a powerful crime lord. They can be found protecting ambassadors and diplomats, veteran politicians and just about anyone who holds power and has enemies.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Security Personnel Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Security Personnel protect a certain group of people or a specific person. As law enforcement agents, they might patrol in pairs or in small teams to respond to crimes and protect innocent villains from violence, robbery, or anything else that would harm them. When faced with a significant threat, Security Personnel double or triple their numbers and supplement their strength with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Security Specialists"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Security_Specialists"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldiers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldiers_(CL_2)"}," as the situation demands.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["In some instances, a security team might include a number of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"},". Patrol Droids might fill in for security forces or accompany them as they make their rounds, likewise, Security Droids can also augment a security force's strength, though Battle Droids and Military Droids are rare after ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},". On the other hand, within the Trade Federation and ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Confederacy of Independent Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Confederacy_of_Independent_Systems","referenceId":"reference:dfc46c9d666b9b41"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," served almost exclusively as security forces.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Security Personnel Statistics (CL 2)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 6\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"http